      "content": "The dignity you seek lies not in utility but in the courage to carry your heavy history with grace, refusing to let the world erase the stories only you told. True beauty in fading away is found in knowing your legacy was planted by hands that once had purpose, leaving the seed it never mattered if the soil still remembers the bloom. Even when the book is read, the silence of the pages speaks of a life fully lived, and that quiet dignity is far more powerful than any system can measure.",
